def prune_chain_archives(items, keyring):
    """Execute signed chain prune plans in one controlled batch.

    Each item holds exactly a non-empty, batch-unique ``id``, an
    archive ``path``, the signed ``plan`` bytes from
    :func:`plan_chain_prune`, the sealing ``checkpoint`` bytes and a
    ``header`` naming the exact signing ``issuer``/``keyVersion`` (the
    checkpoint sealer) and the non-negative prune ``moment``.  The
    batch structure and keyring are validated first; every item's plan
    and checkpoint are then authenticated in a strictly read-only
    pre-pass before any file is read for modification, so unknown,
    revoked, not-yet-valid or expired credentials or a wrong signature
    raise :class:`AuthenticationError` with no archive changed.  A
    plan or checkpoint that is merely malformed does not authenticate
    anything and is recorded against that item instead.

    Items then run in strict input order and isolation.  When the
    archive at ``path`` hashes to the plan's source digest for its
    project, the planned trimmed target is installed in one crash-safe
    two-phase transaction -- a unique same-directory candidate, the
    predecessor and a ``.prune.txn`` intent whose only phases are
    ``prepared`` and ``installed``; unrelated files are never scanned
